gm-method (declarative game-phase FSM via xstate5 ctx.defineGameFSM): ctx.defineGameFSM(spec) compiles a declarative spec to an xstate 5 machine for game-phase orchestration. States with enter/exit/tick/on/after, guarded + multi-target-array transitions, fsm.context is the live xstate context so hook mutation is immediately visible. App calls fsm.tick(dt) from update(ctx,dt). Server + client (singleplayer) via the same dual-import idiom. Pattern: declare game states declaratively, keep tick logic in enter/exit/tick/on hooks, use after: for timeouts, multi-target arrays for branching transitions.